  "privacyTitle": "Privacy Policy",
  "privacyLastUpdated": "Last updated: {date}",
  "@privacyLastUpdated": { "placeholders": { "date": { "type": "String" } } },
  "privacySection1Title": "1. Who we are",
  "privacySection1Body": "ilemO is an independent app created to centralize information about Celestial Church of Christ (CCC) parishes in Benin, with the aim of expanding to other African countries. It is developed and maintained by an independent developer, outside any official administrative structure of the CCC.",
  "privacySection2Title": "2. Data we collect",
  "privacySection2Body": "ilemO is designed to work with as little personal data as possible:\n\n• Location: used only occasionally and locally on your device, to find the parishes closest to you (\"Nearby\" feature). This location is never sent to or stored on our servers.\n\n• Favorites: parishes you mark as favorites are saved only on your device (local storage), and are never transmitted or shared.\n\n• Display preference: your choice of light or dark theme is also stored locally on your device.",
  "privacySection3Title": "3. What we do not collect (for now)",
  "privacySection3Body": "As of today, ilemO does not create a user account, does not ask for your name, email, or phone number, and does not send any push notifications. No identifiable personal data is therefore collected by the app in its current version.",
  "privacySection4Title": "4. Third-party services used",
  "privacySection4Body": "Parish information (name, region, contact, GPS coordinates, etc.) is hosted on Firebase / Google Cloud (Google LLC), which applies its own security and privacy rules. The location and directions feature may rely on Google Maps. These third-party services may, under their own policies, process certain technical data (IP address, device type) necessary for their operation.",
  "privacySection5Title": "5. Your rights",
  "privacySection5Body": "Under Benin's law No. 2017-20 of April 20, 2018 on the Digital Code of the Republic of Benin, relating in particular to the protection of personal data, and under the supervision of the Personal Data Protection Authority (APDP), everyone has a right to access, correct, and delete data concerning them. Since ilemO does not currently collect any identifiable personal data on its servers, exercising these rights mainly applies to data stored locally on your device, which you can delete at any time via the app settings or by uninstalling the app.",
  "privacySection6Title": "6. Future changes to this policy",
  "privacySection6Body": "If new features were to require creating an account, sending notifications, or any other collection of personal data, this privacy policy will be updated beforehand, and the new version will be made available in the app and on this page.",
  "privacySection7Title": "7. Children",
  "privacySection7Body": "ilemO is not intended for targeted use by children and does not knowingly collect any personal data about minors.",
  "privacySection8Title": "8. Contact",
  "privacySection8Body": "For any questions regarding this privacy policy or the ilemO app, you can contact us via the contact information available in the app's \"About\" section.",

